#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
azvpn-cli — headless Azure point-to-site VPN client for Entra-authenticated
gateways. Python 3 stdlib only, drives openvpn3. No sudo, no GUI.

Why this exists
---------------
The Azure VPN Client hardcodes its OAuth *client_id* per cloud and ignores the
profile's <audience>. If your gateway sits behind a custom Entra app, the stock
client is refused with AADSTS650057 — Microsoft's first-party app is not
permitted to request your custom resource. This tool does the OAuth itself,
using the gateway's own <audience> as the client_id, so the problem disappears.

It also outlives the Azure VPN Client for Linux (retired 2026-08-31): it speaks
to the gateway directly and needs no vendor binary.

Why openvpn3 and not openvpn
----------------------------
Azure P2S with Entra auth is plain OpenVPN where the password is an Entra
access token (~2.1 kB). Stock openvpn 2.x packs random material, options,
IV_* peer-info, username and password into a single 2048-byte control-channel
buffer, so it fails before sending anything:

    TLS Error: Key Method #2 write failed

That is a hard structural limit — not tunable via --max-packet-size, and not
avoidable by shortening the username. OpenVPN 3 Core is a separate
implementation without that ceiling; it is also what the Azure VPN Client is
built on. So openvpn3 is required, not preferred.

    openvpn3-linux is LINUX ONLY. There is no openvpn3 CLI for macOS, and
    stock openvpn there hits the same 2048-byte wall.

Everything else comes out of the profile XML Azure gives you:

    <fqdn>          -> remote <fqdn> 443 tcp-client
    <serversecret>  -> 512 hex chars = OpenVPN Static key V1 -> <tls-auth>
    <audience>      -> OAuth client_id, and scope "<audience>/.default"
    <tenant>        -> authority

Nothing organisation-specific is embedded. Point --profile at your own
azurevpnconfig.xml. Safe to share.

Usage
-----
    azvpn-cli up      --profile ~/vpn/eu.xml
    azvpn-cli status  --profile ~/vpn/eu.xml
    azvpn-cli logs    --profile ~/vpn/eu.xml
    azvpn-cli down    --profile ~/vpn/eu.xml
"""

